{
  "_meta": {
    "story": "2.0-B4 T2 — connector mapping",
    "purpose": "Source records in the shape each connector's API actually returns, used to pin every mapper's normalised output.",
    "provenance": "Hand-written from each provider's API contract and from the field sets the AgentIQ connectors already request (servicenow.py INCIDENT_CI_FIELDS + INCIDENT_RESOLUTION_FIELDS + ASSIGNMENT_HISTORY_FIELDS + CMDB_FIELDS; jira.py's requested fields; salesforce.py's SOQL objects). NOT dumped from the mappers, so a mapper regression cannot silently update its own expectations — the same discipline as the 2.0-D3 App Insights golden fixtures.",
    "servicenow_note": "Every field is a {value, display_value} envelope because the connector reads with sysparm_display_value=all. The two halves are deliberately DIFFERENT here (raw '2026-07-01 09:14:22' vs display '01-07-2026 10:14:22' in a non-UTC instance format) so a mapper that reads the wrong half fails the test rather than passing by coincidence.",
    "no_individuals": "The person-shaped fields (assigned_to, caller_id, Jira assignee, Salesforce OwnerId=005...) are PRESENT on purpose: a leak test over a fixture with no individuals in it would be vacuous."
  },

